Package: BCRAT
Title: NCI Breast Cancer Risk Assessment Tool ('Gail Model') for ModelsCloud
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ramin", "Rezaeianzadeh", email = "raminrzn@student.ubc.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mitchell H.", "Gail", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the original breast cancer risk model"))
Description: A self-contained implementation of the NCI Breast Cancer Risk
    Assessment Tool (BCRAT), commonly known as the "Gail model", which
    predicts the 5-year probability of invasive breast cancer from age,
    age at menarche, age at first live birth, number of first-degree
    relatives with breast cancer, number of prior breast biopsies, atypical
    hyperplasia status, and race/ethnicity (Gail et al., J Natl Cancer Inst,
    1989, <doi:10.1093/jnci/81.24.1879>; Costantino et al., J Natl Cancer
    Inst, 1999, <doi:10.1093/jnci/91.18.1541>; Gail et al., J Natl Cancer
    Inst, 2007, <doi:10.1093/jnci/djm223>; Matsuno et al., J Natl Cancer
    Inst, 2011, <doi:10.1093/jnci/djr109>; Banegas et al., J Natl Cancer
    Inst, 2017, <doi:10.1093/jnci/djw215>). The package exposes both the
    vectorised model function bcrat() and the standard ModelsCloud
    prediction API (model_run(), get_sample_input(), get_default_input())
    for interactive use in R or deployment as a hosted model on the
    ModelsCloud platform.
